+## High-complexity function
+
+`handle_request` in `src/smoke/service.py` is the dispatch of the service and the function the
+history touches most. It holds TP-C6. Its intended cyclomatic complexity is above 15 by the
+appsec-review counter (branches, loops, boolean operators and conditional expressions); the
+measured value is recorded in the guide. Note that appsec-review's prioritization batch currently
+lists the Python grammar as unscored (`UNSCORED_GRAMMARS`), which the guide records as a gap.
+
+## Code-intelligence cases
+
+`src/smoke/app.py` carries the appsec-review Python graph-export fixture unchanged: five remote
+paths (SQL, command, path, SSRF, deserialization), an argv and an environment source, a `getpass`
+API source, a sanitized path (`realpath`), a dominating and a non-dominating guard (`ping`),
+virtual dispatch (`Handler.handle`), an unresolved reflective call (`dispatch`), a cross-function
+summary (`run_query`), an unclassified NoSQL sink and an HTTP response sink. The fixed state of
+`read_report` adds a second `realpath` sanitizer and a dominating `startswith` guard.
+
